	(text "DOCK_DET = 3.3 V x (1k + 10k) / (100k + 1k + 10k) = 0.33 V on the perch (10k ID resistor there),\n3.3 V undocked, 0.03 V with the pad shorted to GND. J303 is pin for pin with the dock-pad board."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 262.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fd1915d5-2d01-4fa5-a7ca-1684e8d0c2cb")
	)
	(text_box "Values and why (VIEWE ALL-UEOL018VG-RA31-A001A spec V1.1; TI SLOS854D, SLYS045C, SBOS681; ST DS11811)\n- J301 is mapped like the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75 J3: connector pin k = panel pin 32 - k (table above).\n  MTP_PWR (panel 13) and the MIPI pins (panel 23 to 30) stay open. QSPI on the FSPI IO_MUX pins GPIO9 to 14 (40 MHz).\n- Panel supplies: VCI, IOVCC, VCI_EN, VBAT and TP_3.3V all on DISP_3V3 (TPS22917, power sheet), as on the Waveshare\n  kit, with 4.7 uF + 100 nF at the connector. VBAT takes 3.3 to 5.5 V (VIEWE's reply of 16 October 2026, page 12).\n- Touch bus (I2C1, CST820 0x15): 3.3 V logic with no pull-ups in the panel (VIEWE's reply of 16 October 2026). 4.7k on\n  TP_SDA and TP_SCL and 10k on TP_INT go to DISP_3V3, so switching the panel off leaves no path that back-powers it.\n  TP_RST is push-pull. Firmware drives LCD_RST and TP_RST low before DISP_EN goes low.\n- DRV2605L on +3V3 with EN tied high: SDA, SCL, EN and IN/TRIG may not exceed VDD + 0.3 V (SLOS854D 6.1), so it stays\n  powered while the sensor bus is. Standby by register 4.1 uA (shutdown 4 uA). REG 1 uF, VDD 1 uF + 100 nF, VDD/NC to\n  VDD, IN/TRIG to GND (unused: I2C trigger). LRA 1.8 V rms into 24 ohm is about 75 mA rms (LD0832AA: 90 mA max).\n- TMAG5273A2 (+-133 / +-266 mT, 0x35) sits on the board back at (-28, 0) mm under the magnet track. INT is open drain\n  with a 47k pull-up (wake source on GPIO5), TEST to GND, 100 nF (TI asks for 10 nF or more).\n- LIS2DW12 (0x19): CS tied high selects I2C. SDO/SA0 is an I/O (SPI SDO), so it reaches +3V3 through R309 10k instead\n  of a hard tie to the regulator output; ST's internal 20 to 30k SA0 pull-up is in parallel. RES to GND. INT1 is push-pull\n  (default low): firmware sets it active low before deep sleep. 100 nF + 1 uF at VDD and VDD_IO.\n- OPT3001 (0x44): ADDR and the thermal pad to GND, INT unused (polled), 100 nF at VDD.\n- Sensor bus (I2C0, GPIO42 SDA, GPIO41 SCL): 4.7k to +3V3. Every device on it runs from +3V3: TMAG5273A2 0x35,\n  MAX17048 0x36 (power sheet), LIS2DW12 0x19, OPT3001 0x44, DRV2605L 0x5A.\n- Dock link: SMF5.0A on VBUS_DOCK; D102 (power sheet) ORs it into VIN_CHG, so dock and USB never feed each other.\n  DOCK_DET on GPIO1 (ADC1_CH0, RTC wake): R308 100k pull-up, R307 1k and the LESD5D5.0 ESD diode protect the pin on an\n  exposed contact, C310 100 nF filters the ADC input. Docked only when DOCK_DET reads 150 to 600 mV and CHG_PGOOD is low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 165.1 0)
		(size 137.16 47.86)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27)
